  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nThe vulnerability stems from how the contract handles the remaining \"dust\" from an order after it's been rounded down to the nearest lotSize. Here is the step-by-step flow that leads to the incorrect revert:\n\n* User Action: A user calls `postFillOrder` to submit a Fill-or-Kill (FOK) order. Let's assume the market `lotSize` is 100 and the user wants to buy 199 units.\n\n* Order Creation: The `_processFillBidOrder` function creates a temporary order in memory, `newOrder`, where `newOrder.amount` is 199.\n\n* Matching Logic: This function then calls the internal matching logic (`_matchIncomingBid`), passing newOrder as an argument. Crucially, because [`newOrder`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/main/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L347) is a memory struct, it's passed by reference, not as a copy. Any change to the order inside the matching logic will affect the original `newOrder`.\n\n* Rounding: Inside the `_matchIncomingOrder` function, the code calculates the fillable amount, which is rounded down to the nearest `lotSize`.\n\n    fillableAmount = (199 / 100) * 100 which results in 100.\n\n* State Update: The matching logic then updates the amount of the user's order that is still left to be filled:\n\n    - incomingOrder.amount -= fillableAmount; (which is 199 - 100).\n    - Because `incomingOrder` is a reference to `newOrder`, the value of newOrder.amount is now updated to 99.\n\n* Incorrect Revert: The matching logic finishes, and control returns to the `_processFillBidOrder` function. The code now performs the FOK check: [`if (... && newOrder.amount > 0)`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/main/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L440).\n\n    - Since `newOrder.amount` is now 99, the condition is true.\n    - The transaction incorrectly reverts with `FOKOrderNotFilled()`, even though the only amount left unfilled was the dust from rounding, which the specification says should be ignored.\n\n# Recommended mitigation steps\nModify the FOK order check to only revert if the remaining unfilled amount is greater than or equal to one lotSize.\n\n```diff\n\n// contracts/clob/CLOB.sol\n-   if (args.fillOrderType == FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL && newOrder.amount > 0) revert FOKOrderNotFilled();\n+   if (args.fillOrderType == FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL && newOrder.amount >= ds.settings().lotSizeInBase) revert FOKOrderNotFilled();\n\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "This test file `PoC_FOKOrderIncorrectlyReverts.t.sol` can be placed in `test/c4-poc/`:\n\n```solidity\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase} from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB, Side} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\nimport {CLOB} from \"contracts/clob/CLOB.sol\";\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"test/harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\n\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n    // Helper function to set up user token balances for tests\n    function _setupTokens(address clob, Side side, address user, uint256 amount, uint256 price) internal {\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        ERC20Harness quoteToken = ERC20Harness(ICLOB(clob).getQuoteToken());\n        ERC20Harness baseToken = ERC20Harness(ICLOB(clob).getBaseToken());\n\n        if (side == Side.BUY) {\n            uint256 depositAmount = ICLOB(clob).getQuoteTokenAmount(price, amount);\n            quoteToken.mint(user, depositAmount);\n            quoteToken.approve(address(accountManager), depositAmount);\n            accountManager.deposit(user, address(quoteToken), depositAmount);\n        } else {\n            uint256 depositAmount = amount;\n            baseToken.mint(user, depositAmount);\n            baseToken.approve(address(accountManager), depositAmount);\n            accountManager.deposit(user, address(baseToken), depositAmount);\n        }\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    // Helper function to place a simple limit order for tests\n    function _setupOrder(address clob, Side side, address user, uint256 amountInBase, uint256 price)\n        internal\n        returns (ICLOB.PostLimitOrderResult memory)\n    {\n        _setupTokens(clob, side, user, amountInBase, price);\n        ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory args = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase: amountInBase,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            price: price,\n            cancelTimestamp: 0,\n            side: side,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        });\n        vm.prank(user);\n        return ICLOB(clob).postLimitOrder(user, args);\n    }\n\n    function test_PoC_FOKOrderIncorrectlyReverts() external {\n        address maker = rite;\n        address taker = jb;\n        CLOB market = CLOB(abCLOB);\n\n        uint256 lotSize = 1 ether;\n        vm.prank(address(clobManager)); // Prank as the manager contract to call the admin function\n        market.setLotSizeInBase(lotSize);\n\n        _setupOrder(address(market), Side.SELL, maker, 2 ether, 1 ether);\n        _setupTokens(address(market), Side.BUY, taker, 1.9 ether, 1 ether);\n\n        ICLOB.PostFillOrderArgs memory fillArgs = ICLOB.PostFillOrderArgs({\n            amount: 1.9 ether,\n            priceLimit: 1 ether,\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            amountIsBase: true,\n            fillOrderType: ICLOB.FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL\n        });\n\n        vm.expectRevert(CLOB.FOKOrderNotFilled.selector);\n        vm.prank(taker);\n        market.postFillOrder(taker, fillArgs);\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nRun the test case with `forge test --mt test_PoC_FOKOrderIncorrectlyReverts -vv`, which should output:\n\n```text\n\nRan 1 test for test/c4-poc/PoC_FOKOrderIncorrectlyReverts.t.sol:PoC\n[PASS] test_PoC_FOKOrderIncorrectlyReverts() (gas: 610885)\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 10.31ms (1.24ms CPU time)\n\n```",
